 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Intended uses: a voltage reference in a regulated supply, or a clamp guarding a circuit against overvoltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Test current",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Types from 2.0 V to 36 V are specified at IZT = 5 mA; types from 39 V to 75 V at IZT = 2.5 mA. ZZT is given at the same current as VZ."
  },
  {
   "topic": "MM1Z47B",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Type code B6. VZ is 47 V nominal, 46.06 V min and 47.94 V max at IZT = 2.5 mA; ZZT is 150 Ω max at that current; IR is 2 µA at VR = 36 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Voltage window and impedance",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Each type has a VZ min and max either side of nominal (MM1Z10B: 9.8 V to 10.2 V). ZZT is 30 Ω for the 6.8 V to 11 V types, 100 Ω at 2.0 V and 300 Ω at 75 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reverse leakage",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "IR is 120 µA for the 2.0 V to 2.7 V types, falls to 0.1 µA for 10 V to 36 V, and is 2 µA, 1 µA and 0.2 µA for the higher types, each at its own VR."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Rated dissipation is 500 mW up to an ambient of 75 °C and falls in a straight line to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Transient thermal impedance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Thermal impedance rises from about 26 °C/W for a 10 ms pulse to about 110 °C/W near 0.1 s and levels off around 450 °C/W for pulses of tens of seconds."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity level 1 per J-STD-020, lead-free reflow peak 260 °C. Mold compound rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen free. Terminals are solder plated and meet MIL-STD-750 Method 2026 solderability. A band on the body marks the cathode."
  }
 ],
